taylor_support: Customer report - structured/json mode responses intermittently fail to parse. Parser error: "Unexpected token \u0000 in JSON at position 0" when feeding response to JSON.parse. Happened after streaming large completions with many emojis. Attaching sample stream capture.

support-bot: Ticket #CS-4821 created and assigned to eng. :robot_face:

akshat_repro: Repro steps I ran locally:
1) curl -s -D- -o - --http1.1 -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate -H 'Authorization: Bearer ...' -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"model":"gpt-large","mode":"structured","input":"repeat \"quote\" and emojis \uD83D\uDE00 many times"}' | tee stream.txt
2) parse with node: JSON.parse(stream.txt)

akshat_repro: Capture shows chunk boundaries splitting escape sequences. Example chunks:
```
chunk1: "{\"items\":[\"hello \""
chunk2: "world\",\"\\uD83D\\uDE00\"]}"
```
When concatenated naively, the surrogate pair gets split and the leading quote near 'world' sometimes gets lost due to off-by-one. Results in 'hello \"world' missing quote.

jordan_eng: :eyes: This looks like streaming flush truncates mid-UTF8/escape. Two issues: 1) streaming layer doesn't guarantee chunk atomicity for escaped sequences, 2) serializer may be dropping a leading quote when buffer boundary aligns with quote+backslash. Can you paste the raw hex around the split? Also what runtime (hosted/dedicated/private)?

taylor_support: Customer on hosted, region us-west1. Raw hex around split (from stream.txt): ... 22 5c 75 44 38 33 44 5c 75 44 45 30 30 22 2c ... (quote backslash u D8 3D backslash u DE 00 quote comma)

jordan_eng: Suggest mitigation: implement chunk-assembler that ensures we don't break on backslash or high-bit bytes. Short-term, recommend rerouting through text-mode and then run our structured-extract post-processing. I'll prepare a hotfix to the streaming serializer to buffer at least 8 bytes beyond last backslash.

sami_infra: Will schedule runtime patch for hosted/dedicated tomorrow. For immediate customer unblock, taylor, send them the small proxy script to reassemble stream (node example):
```
const net = require('net');
let carry = '';
process.stdin.on('data', (b)=>{
  const s = carry + b.toString('utf8');
  const safe = s.replace(/\\u([0-9a-fA-F]{0,3})$/,'');
  const m = s.match(/\\u([0-9a-fA-F]{0,3})$/);
  carry = m ? m[0] : '';
  process.stdout.write(safe);
});
```

taylor_support: Sending proxy now. Customer confirmed parsing succeeded after proxy. Marking P1 but mitigated. :white_check_mark:

akshat_repro: I'll add unit test for chunk boundaries and surrogate pairs. Also adding log that warns when a chunk ends with a single backslash.

jordan_eng: Thanks. We'll track patch rollout and add a regression test in the streaming suite. :thumbsup:
